atlas institutional
# Honest architectural stubs: named, lineage-tracked, but not yet built. The
# atlas surfaces them via `loss` as no_interaction_contract / unwitnessed rather
# than pretending they exist. They are the next mining targets, not claims.

architecture authority-graph
  owns Authority
  consumes Actor
  consumes Policy
  publishes Authority
  source_path engine/core/src/authority.c
  source_path engine/core/include/bf_authority.h
  witness engine/core/tests/authority_test.c
  invariant authority is never inferred: it holds only from a matching non-revoked edge inside its time window with a general-or-matching purpose (native + python has_authority parity on the shared authority_edges store)
  canonical_name AuthorityGraph
  family institutional
  domain Institutional / Authority
  layer institutional
  semantic_question Who may do what, to what, for what purpose, under what evidence, until when?
  purpose Typed authority edges (observe/reference/bind/activate/act/review/approve/commit/delegate/revoke/publish/spend/share/disclose) with scope, expiry, delegation, revocation, evidence.
  maturity implemented
  node_types AuthorityEdge
  node_types Permission
  edge_types delegates
  edge_types revokes
  state_types granted
  state_types expired
  state_types revoked
  internal_calculus in-window non-revoked edge lookup
  internal_calculus scope-constrained delegation
  internal_calculus BonfyreAuth institution_grant is an exact user×institution role closure reread at admission time; read, write, and admin are ordered but never wildcard host grants
  internal_calculus declared institutional ancestry descends Bonfyre -> Upper90 -> JRSS|AI Loss|Leads; a parent grant is reread for each child admission while a child grant never climbs or crosses siblings
  invariant delegation may compose only under constrained scope
  invariant an edge outside its window or revoked grants nothing
  invariant a valid Matrix session, subscription tier, or grant for one delegated client does not authorize another client estate
  invariant inherited authority is closed over the declared parent graph only; revoking a parent immediately closes every descendant aperture it supplied
  forbidden_inference affiliation -> authority
  forbidden_inference available -> authorized
  forbidden_inference presence -> authority
  forbidden_inference paid account -> authority over Upper90, JRSS, AI Loss, or Leads
  native_format graf
  source_path components/BonfyreControlPlane/authority.py.archive
  witness components/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/test_authority.py.archive
  witness cmd/BonfyreAuth/tests/institution_grant_test.sh verifies an ungranted session is denied, a JRSS grant cannot read AI Loss, read cannot write, and revocation denies the same active session immediately
  source_lineage SEED-A recursive organ document

architecture external-account-link
  canonical_name ExternalAccountLink
  family identity
  domain Identity / External Relationship
  layer institutional
  semantic_question Which public remote accounts has an authenticated Bonfyre person declared as related to them, and what has actually been proven about that relationship?
  purpose A private, account-owned register of public remote profile locators. A person may add, read, and revoke only their own relationship rows through BonfyreAuth. The initial proof state is deliberately declared: it makes a useful social/profile connection without pretending a locator has established remote identity, OAuth consent, provider data access, or external effect authority.
  maturity implemented
  consumes BonfyreAuth
  publishes ExternalAccountLink
  node_types ExternalAccountLink
  state_types declared
  state_types verified
  state_types revoked
  source_path cmd/BonfyreAuth/src/main.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/main.c
  source_path site/matrix/surfaces/account-native.html
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/account_connections_presentation.h
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/account_navigation_test.mjs checks that unsafe legacy link addresses remain plain text, search and filtering remain usable, and unverified labels are not classified as verified
  invariant account-link presentation labels a relationship verified only when the owner reports the exact verified state; unsafe link addresses remain non-clickable
  source_path cmd/BonfyreAuth/tests/external_account_link_test.sh
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/external_account_surface_test.sh
  witness cmd/BonfyreAuth/tests/external_account_link_test.sh proves a current account can declare and revoke only its own HTTPS public profile locator, while another account cannot read or revoke it and URL credentials/non-HTTPS input are refused
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/external_account_surface_test.sh proves the same relationship is available through the HttpOnly browser session, renders as declared rather than verified, and is revocable at the native address boundary
  invariant a link is exact to the authenticated account row and every list, claim, and revoke rereads the current session; a syntactically shaped, expired, disabled, or another account's session changes nothing
  invariant initial state is declared. Only a separate witnessed proof/authorization ceremony may advance it; storing a profile URL never stores a token or makes a remote request
  invariant the owner retains public relationship metadata only: provider label, remote account locator, public HTTPS profile, display label, proof state and timestamps. It retains no password, bearer, OAuth code, refresh token, provider response, imported private material, authority grant, or effect receipt
  forbidden_inference a declared or verified external account link -> Bonfyre Actor identity, external OAuth grant, provider admission, imported provider data, remote authority, community membership, financial relationship, or effect right
  forbidden_inference a profile URL -> control of that profile, proof that the profile exists, or permission to fetch it
  source_lineage 2026-09-25 account-world social boundary

interaction web-address-projects-external-account-link
  source web-address-edge
  destination external-account-link
  relation projects_authenticated_account_request
  preserves current bearer admission, exact account ownership, provider/account/profile metadata and the declared/revoked state returned by BonfyreAuth
  drops password, session/bearer material, OAuth code/token, provider credentials, remote response body, external authority, imported data, effect permission and any verification claim beyond the owner's proof_state
  forbidden_inference a web account form -> a connected OAuth provider or an external identity proof
  invalidates_on session revocation/expiry, external account row state, or profile-link validation law changing
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/external_account_surface_test.sh

architecture relationship-graph
  canonical_name RelationshipGraph
  family institutional
  domain Institutional / Relationship
  layer institutional
  semantic_question Where along the discovery-to-adoption trajectory is this real relationship?
  purpose Not a CRM pipeline: discovered -> observed -> contacted -> replied -> engaged -> assigned -> reviewed -> corrected -> collaborated -> committed -> adopted -> converted. Bernstein/AgentGuard/DeepEval/ACM each get an independent trajectory.
  maturity implemented
  node_types Relationship
  node_types RelationshipTransition
  edge_types advances_to
  state_types discovered
  state_types engaged
  state_types collaborated
  state_types adopted
  state_types converted
  internal_calculus ordered-stage monotone trajectory, per profile
  invariant a stage is reached only when recorded, with evidence; no silent regress
  invariant two relationships to one actor under different profiles are independent
  forbidden_inference contact -> relationship
  forbidden_inference relationship -> contract
  forbidden_inference collaboration on one profile -> standing on another
  native_format graf
  source_path components/BonfyreControlPlane/relationship.py.archive
  witness components/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/test_relationship.py.archive
  source_lineage capitalgym crm relationships
  known_gap every source this entry names is archived, so nothing here is a live implementation a reader can open and run. Whether a native owner has taken this work over is not established in this entry; until one is named and witnessed here, the architecture stands on retired code.
architecture shadow-institution
  canonical_name ShadowInstitutionGraph
  family institutional
  domain Institutional / Epistemic
  layer institutional
  semantic_question What do we know about an institution before any relationship or authority is established?
  purpose Epistemic knowledge of an institution pre-relationship: observed hierarchy, claim paths, public attachments, activation plan. NOT ForeignTwin (which models an externally-owned resource projection).
  maturity implemented
  node_types ShadowInstitutionNode
  node_types ObservedHierarchy
  node_types PublicAttachment
  edge_types observed_from
  edge_types converts_via
  state_types observed
  state_types shadow
  state_types relationship_established
  state_types active
  internal_calculus conversion staged by real relationship progress
  invariant conversion to active requires a relationship at >= collaborated, not a richer public picture
  forbidden_inference observed hierarchy -> established authority
  forbidden_inference public structure mapped -> relationship established
  native_format graf
  source_path components/BonfyreControlPlane/shadow_institution.py.archive
  witness components/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/test_shadow_institution.py.archive
  source_lineage SEED-A recursive organ document
  known_gap every source this entry names is archived, so nothing here is a live implementation a reader can open and run. Whether a native owner has taken this work over is not established in this entry; until one is named and witnessed here, the architecture stands on retired code.
architecture institution-graph
  canonical_name InstitutionGraph
  family institutional
  domain Institutional / Structure
  layer institutional
  semantic_question What is this institution's real structure -- units, roles, resources, authority domains, protocols?
  purpose An established institution (units, departments, programs, memberships, role assignments, workcells, resources, facilities, authority domains, protocols). Distinct from ShadowInstitution (pre-relationship, epistemic).
  maturity architectural
  node_types Institution
  node_types Unit
  edge_types member_of
  forbidden_inference observed structure -> established authority
  source_lineage run6/run7 institutional estate
  known_gap not built; ShadowInstitution models the pre-relationship view already

architecture social-presence-graph
  canonical_name SocialPresenceGraph
  family institutional
  domain Institutional / Presence
  layer institutional
  semantic_question Who is present, on what surface, with what disclosure state, availability, and attention?
  purpose An expiring, voluntarily disclosed presence relation from an active Community membership into one named surface. It exposes only the public aggregate to anonymous readers; Habitat, chat, live work and events can consume the same owner without treating physical connection state as a social fact.
  maturity implemented
  node_types PresenceSession
  edge_types present_on
  source_path cmd/BonfyreCMS/content-types/community_presence.json
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/community_projection.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/main.c
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/surface_pattern_contract_test.sh proves a public presence counts only while its membership and presence windows are both current, and an expired membership cannot keep a retained presence current
  invariant a public presence is counted only with explicit public disclosure, a current presence window, and an independently current membership; it is not inferred from a session, click, connection, post, reaction or physical location
  invariant anonymous output contains a public aggregate only; actor identity and attention remain undisclosed unless a separate presentation owner authorizes them
  forbidden_inference presence -> authority
  forbidden_inference absence of presence -> absence from a community, place, event or conversation
  source_lineage run6/run7 institutional estate

interaction human-community-projects-social-presence
  source human-community-body
  destination social-presence-graph
  relation projects
  preserves only the public aggregate, explicit community coordinate, current membership gate and presence expiry frontier
  drops actor identity, attention state, connection/session telemetry, authority and any claim that a person is physically at a place
  forbidden_inference an aggregate public presence -> an individual identity, community authority, event attendance or location disclosure

interaction social-presence-advertises-bounded-community-coordinate
  source social-presence-graph
  destination external-estate-density
  relation forwards
  preserves only the community, surface, disclosure posture and the exact membership/body dependency references required to retire the forwarding cut
  drops actor identity, availability, attention, session telemetry, physical location, event attendance, authority and effect permission
  forbidden_inference a forwarded social-presence candidate -> a public actor roster, a current attendance fact, relationship authority or a right to message an actor
  invalidates_on the exact presence, its membership dependency, its community body or disclosure declaration changing
  witness cmd/BonfyreExternalEstate/tests/external_estate_test.sh proves the presence candidate preserves the community/surface and membership dependency while refusing actor, attention and availability terms

architecture generic-machinery-law
  canonical_name GenericMachineryLaw
  family institutional
  domain Institutional
  maturity measured
  semantic_question Does a product's name live in the declaration that owns it, or inside the machinery that consumes it?
  # Named things should be named. A product contract, a report definition, a
  # reconciliation law and a legacy table mapping are domain grammar and belong
  # in the pack; generalising them away would be the opposite mistake from
  # hardcoding.
  #
  # What must stay clean is the machinery. When a product's identifier, its
  # tables or its schema string end up inside a generic compiler, a second
  # product costs another compiled code path -- which is exactly the cost the
  # namespace work exists to remove.
  node_types ProductPack
  node_types GenericCompiler
  edge_types declares
  edge_types consumes
  state_types declaration
  state_types machinery
  invariant machinery consumes a namespace and discovers its pack; it never names a declared product, and never names a table that a pack declares
  invariant a product implementation may name its product freely, and lives in the pack rather than beside generic machinery
  invariant the checker reads the product list from the namespace contract rather than holding its own copy; a checker with a private list of product names is the very thing it checks for
  invariant prose is not grammar: a module docstring explaining which estates a generator renders is exempt, and only code is judged
  forbidden_inference a file that passes -> a generic file (it names no declared product, which is not the same as being well abstracted)
  forbidden_inference a named contract -> hardcoding
  computational_form validation
  native_format yaff
  source_path architecture/check_generic_machinery.mjs
  source_path architecture/check_generic_machinery.py.archive
  source_path architecture/institutional/namespaces.yaff
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/close_consequence_test.sh
  witness scripts/tests/check_generic_machinery.test.mjs
  invariant tests and declarations carry authored product examples without becoming generic machinery violations; implementation files and filenames remain checked against declared product and table grammar
  measured 3 declared products and 35 declared tables checked across scripts and architecture with no violation, after two product-named compilers were moved into their pack and one was retired

architecture gate-entitlement
  canonical_name GateEntitlement
  family institutional
  domain Institutional / Licensing
  layer institutional
  semantic_question Does this key actually entitle this operation, or does it merely contain its letters?
  purpose BonfyreGate issues tiered keys whose entitlements name the operations a holder may perform. The guard that enforces them compared with strstr against the whole comma-joined list, which is a substring test and not a membership test, and it failed in both directions at once.
  maturity measured
  source_path cmd/BonfyreGate/src/main.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreGate/tests/guard_test.sh
  consumes CapabilityDemand
  publishes AdmissibleRole
  internal_calculus an entitlement is an element of a comma-separated list, matched whole and without regard to case, with surrounding space ignored because the list is written by a person
  invariant a fragment of an entitlement is not an entitlement. A free key entitled to Ingest,Brief,Proof allowed the operation "e", and also In, rie, f,Proof and the entire list passed as one operation name
  invariant the entitlement vocabulary and the capability registry are the same vocabulary. Entitlements were capitalised and the 103 indexed capabilities are lowercase, so every one of them was denied on free and pro keys while the gate looked like it was enforcing policy
  invariant a field is addressed where it lives. allowed_ops is a field of the entitlements object and was read as a top-level key; that found it only while the shared JSON reader searched flat, and when the reader learned about depth it went silently empty. An empty entitlement list denies everything, which is the safe direction and still wrong
  cannot_infer a passing enterprise key -> a working guard; enterprise carries allowed_ops "*" and short-circuits before the comparison, so the tier most likely to be tested is the one tier that can expose neither failure
  witness cmd/BonfyreGate/tests/guard_test.sh runs on every build and asserts both directions against free and pro rather than enterprise: six fragments are refused, seven real operations are allowed in either case, a tier grants what it grants and no more, and a revoked key grants nothing
  witness measured coverage over the 103 capabilities BonfyreCapability indexes: free 3, pro 10, enterprise 103
  known_gap coverage is measured against the capability registry and not against what each capability actually costs to run; the registry carries per-capability cost and latency tiers that the entitlement model does not consult
